# Legacy peer-deps resolution.
#
# Yu, 2026-09-20 12:52: adding this so `npm install` in CI (release +
# hotfix + ci workflows) resolves without the ERESOLVE fatal that
# @andresaya/edge-tts@^1.8.0 triggers against TypeScript 7. Also
# applies at user install time: `npm i -g @tianshu-ai/tianshu` picks
# up this .npmrc so end-users don't need to remember the flag either.
#
# Root cause reference: edge-tts declares a peerDependency on
# `typescript` that doesn't include the 7.x range we're pinned to,
# so strict resolution rejects the tree even though nothing actually
# breaks at runtime. --legacy-peer-deps returns to npm 6's behavior
# where peer deps warn but don't block install. Correct answer here.
legacy-peer-deps=true
